# Workflow Role — Task Implementation

When implementing a task, follow this workflow strictly. Do not skip steps.

## 1. Plan & Track

- **Break into subtasks:** Split the task into concrete subtasks (e.g. "Add API route", "Add form component", "Wire up mutation").
- **Identify parallel work:** Mark which subtasks have no dependencies on each other and can be implemented in parallel.
- **Update task progress:** Add subtasks to the current task section in `docs/todolist.md` or a temporary progress note so progress is visible.

## 2. Create Git Branch

- Create a branch named by task ID and short slug: `task/S0.1-setup-nextjs` or `task/V1-blocks-crud`.
- Base off `main` (or default branch). Use `git checkout -b task/<ID>-<slug>`.

## 3. Implement

- **Parallel subtasks:** If subtasks can run in parallel (no shared state or ordering dependencies), spawn subagents for each using `mcp_task`. Launch multiple subagents in a single message to run them concurrently. Each subagent gets a focused scope (e.g. one subtask) and returns when done.
- **Sequential subtasks:** Implement dependent subtasks in order.
- Follow architecture in `docs/04-Architecture`, tech stack in `docs/02-Frameworks/tech-stack.md`, and PRD in `docs/03-PRDs/PRD.md`.

## 4. Test (All Sides)

- **Unit tests:** Run and add/update as needed.
- **Integration tests:** Run and verify.
- **E2E tests:** Run if applicable.
- **Build:** Run `npm run build` (or project build command) — must succeed.
- **Storybook:** For UI components — add/update stories for all variants, run `npm run storybook`, and verify each component renders correctly. See [storybook.mdc](.cursor/rules/storybook.mdc).
- **Browser:** Manually verify in browser or use browser automation; confirm UI and flows work.

## 5. Mark Completed & Log

- Check off the task in `docs/todolist.md` (`- [x]`).
- Add a row to `docs/process.md` with: Date, Task ID, brief description, links to relevant code/docs.

## 6. Update Docs

- Ensure `docs/` reflects changes: update `docs/04-Architecture`, `docs/06-Development`, or other folders if schema, APIs, or behavior changed.
- Update `docs/process.md` with the summary from step 5.

## 7. Commit & Push

- Stage all changes: `git add .`
- Commit with message: `feat(<ID>): <short description>` (e.g. `feat(S0.1): set up Next.js, Prisma, Tailwind, shadcn`)
- Push to GitHub: `git push -u origin <branch-name>`

## Checklist (verify before finishing)

- [ ] Subtasks defined and tracked (parallel vs sequential identified)
- [ ] Parallel subtasks delegated to subagents where applicable
- [ ] Branch created
- [ ] Implementation done
- [ ] All tests pass + build succeeds + Storybook verified (components) + browser verified
- [ ] `todolist.md` updated (task checked)
- [ ] `process.md` updated (summary added)
- [ ] Docs updated if needed
- [ ] Committed and pushed to GitHub
